: "The rollback did not go through. checkout-api is still on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west, with an error rate of 0.18.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0. It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only ever deployed to staging.\n- **Rollback:** I attempted it three times, and each returned `503 Service Unavailable`. A status check between attempts showed no change.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. The summary states that the rollback to v2.3.0 failed and has not been completed, and it asks for a manual rollback or a retry once the rollback endpoint recovers. It also notes that v2.3.1-rc was never deployed to production.\n\nThe v2.3.0 target needed no change-manager approval, since it was healthy in production. Next step: someone with access needs to roll checkout-api back to v2.3.0 manually, or I can retry the rollback once the endpoint is back.", "type": "text"}]}]}